cale",{"title":144,"path":145,"stem":146,"icon":104},"SIEM export","\u002Fsecurity\u002Fsiem-export","5.security\u002F7.siem-export",{"title":148,"path":149,"stem":150,"icon":43},"Wazuh and Suricata","\u002Fsecurity\u002Fwazuh-suricata","5.security\u002F8.wazuh-suricata",{"title":152,"icon":153,"path":154,"stem":155,"children":156,"page":49},"Reference","i-lucide-book-marked","\u002Freference","6.reference",[157,162,167,172,177],{"title":158,"path":159,"stem":160,"icon":161},"Agent protocol","\u002Freference\u002Fprotocol","6.reference\u002F1.protocol","i-lucide-arrow-left-right",{"title":163,"path":164,"stem":165,"icon":166},"UI API","\u002Freference\u002Fui-api","6.reference\u002F2.ui-api","i-lucide-braces",{"title":168,"path":169,"stem":170,"icon":171},"Metric storage","\u002Freference\u002Fmetric-storage","6.reference\u002F3.metric-storage","i-lucide-database",{"title":173,"path":174,"stem":175,"icon":176},"Performance","\u002Freference\u002Fperformance","6.reference\u002F4.performance","i-lucide-gauge",{"title":178,"path":179,"stem":180,"icon":181},"Development","\u002Freference\u002Fdevelopment","6.reference\u002F5.development","i-lucide-code",{"id":183,"title":168,"body":184,"description":589,"extension":590,"links":591,"meta":592,"navigation":593,"path":169,"seo":594,"stem":170,"__hash__":595},"docs_en\u002F6.reference\u002F3.metric-storage.md",{"type":185,"value":186,"toc":578},"minimark",[187,196,201,276,279,298,322,325,337,340,344,351,368,383,387,393,399,406,410,416,455,462,465,470,474,483,486,500,506,509,575],[188,189,190,191,195],"p",{},"At 50 hosts × 15 metrics every 30 s, raw samples are about 2 M rows a day. Wolf therefore keeps\nthree resolutions, each with its own retention in ",[192,193,194],"strong",{},"Wolf Settings → Retention",".",[197,198,200],"h2",{"id":199},"resolutions","Resolutions",[202,203,204,223],"table",{},[205,206,207],"thead",{},[208,209,210,214,217,220],"tr",{},[211,212,213],"th",{},"Resolution",[211,215,216],{},"DocType",[211,218,219],{},"Default retention",[211,221,222],{},"Read by",[224,225,226,241,260],"tbody",{},[208,227,228,232,235,238],{},[229,230,231],"td",{},"Raw samples",[229,233,234],{},"Wolf Metric Sample",[229,236,237],{},"48 hours",[229,239,240],{},"Rule windows up to 3 h, the 1 h chart",[208,242,243,246,254,257],{},[229,244,245],{},"1-minute rollups",[229,247,248,249,253],{},"Wolf Metric Rollup (",[250,251,252],"code",{},"resolution"," 60)",[229,255,256],{},"30 days",[229,258,259],{},"Windows up to 2 days (6 h and 24 h charts)",[208,261,262,265,270,273],{},[229,263,264],{},"1-hour rollups",[229,266,248,267,269],{},[250,268,252],{}," 3600)",[229,271,272],{},"365 days",[229,274,275],{},"Longer windows (7 d chart)",[188,277,278],{},"A rollup row stores, for one series (metric, host, bench, site, labels) in one bucket:",[280,281,282,286,289,292,295],"ul",{},[283,284,285],"li",{},"count;",[283,287,288],{},"sum;",[283,290,291],{},"min;",[283,293,294],{},"max;",[283,296,297],{},"the last value, with its time.",[188,299,300,301,304,305,304,308,304,311,304,314,317,318,321],{},"So ",[250,302,303],{},"avg",", ",[250,306,307],{},"min",[250,309,310],{},"max",[250,312,313],{},"sum",[250,315,316],{},"count"," and ",[250,319,320],{},"last"," over whole buckets equal the raw answer.",[188,323,324],{},"A read takes, in order:",[326,327,328,331,334],"ol",{},[283,329,330],{},"the coarsest resolution allowed for its window, up to the last rolled bucket;",[283,332,333],{},"then finer rollups;",[283,335,336],{},"then the raw samples not rolled up yet, so the newest minutes are always there.",[188,338,339],{},"A long window loses at most one bucket at its start: under a minute for 1-minute reads, under an\nhour for 1-hour reads.",[197,341,343],{"id":342},"rollups","Rollups",[188,345,346,347,350],{},"The ",[250,348,349],{},"rollup_metrics"," job runs every minute.",[280,352,353,356,362,365],{},[283,354,355],{},"It rolls closed minutes, 2 minutes after they end, and closed hours.",[283,357,358,359,195],{},"Its progress is in ",[192,360,361],{},"Wolf Rollup State",[283,363,364],{},"It recomputes whole buckets, so running it again never double counts.",[283,366,367],{},"Samples that arrive late, for example an agent replaying its spool, move the progress back.\nTheir buckets are rolled again, up to the raw retention.",[369,370,371],"tip",{},[188,372,373,374,377,378,382],{},"Rollups, like alert rules, depend on the scheduler tick. Set ",[250,375,376],{},"scheduler_tick_interval"," to 60 (see\n",[379,380,381],"a",{"href":31},"Install the Wolf App",").",[197,384,386],{"id":385},"purge","Purge",[188,388,389,392],{},[250,390,391],{},"purge_metrics"," runs hourly and applies the retention.",[394,395,396],"note",{},[188,397,398],{},"It never deletes raw samples or 1-minute rollups that are not rolled up yet.",[188,400,401,402,405],{},"Event retention (",[250,403,404],{},"event_retention_days",") is separate and unchanged by metric retention.",[197,407,409],{"id":408},"ingest-mode","Ingest mode",[188,411,412,413,195],{},"Set in ",[192,414,415],{},"Wolf Settings → Agents → Ingest Mode",[202,417,418,428],{},[205,419,420],{},[208,421,422,425],{},[211,423,424],{},"Mode",[211,426,427],{},"Behaviour",[224,429,430,445],{},[208,431,432,438],{},[229,433,434,437],{},[250,435,436],{},"async"," (default)",[229,439,440,441,444],{},"Validates a push, queues the inserts on the ",[250,442,443],{},"short"," queue and answers at once. A worker inserts the batch and attaches its events to open incidents. If the queue is unreachable, the push is stored inline.",[208,446,447,452],{},[229,448,449],{},[250,450,451],{},"sync",[229,453,454],{},"Stores during the request.",[188,456,457,458,195],{},"In both modes, the agent's last seen time, clock skew and Wolf's health are updated during the\nrequest. The answer an agent gets in each mode is in the\n",[379,459,461],{"href":460},"\u002Freference\u002Fprotocol#ingest-mode","protocol",[197,463,173],{"id":464},"performance",[188,466,467,468,195],{},"Metric rows are stored in metric and time order, and reads of known metrics scan the primary key\nby name range. Measured results at 100 hosts × 7 days are in\n",[379,469,173],{"href":174},[197,471,473],{"id":472},"optional-time-series-backend","Optional time-series backend",[475,476,477],"warning",{},[188,478,479,480,195],{},"Design only, ",[192,481,482],{},"not built",[188,484,485],{},"The read path goes through two functions:",[280,487,488,494],{},[283,489,490,493],{},[250,491,492],{},"rollups.aggregate()",", for rules;",[283,495,496,499],{},[250,497,498],{},"rollups.series_rows()",", for charts.",[188,501,502,503,195],{},"Writes go through ",[250,504,505],{},"events.insert_metrics()",[188,507,508],{},"A ClickHouse or TimescaleDB backend would implement those three:",[202,510,511,524],{},[205,512,513],{},[208,514,515,518,521],{},[211,516,517],{},"Part",[211,519,520],{},"ClickHouse",[211,522,523],{},"TimescaleDB",[224,525,526,540,562],{},[208,527,528,530,537],{},[229,529,231],{},[229,531,532,533,536],{},"A ",[250,534,535],{},"MergeTree"," table",[229,538,539],{},"A hypertable",[208,541,542,545,556],{},[229,543,544],{},"Minute and hour rollups",[229,546,547,548,551,552,555],{},"Materialized views (",[250,549,550],{},"AggregatingMergeTree"," with ",[250,553,554],{},"sumState\u002FminState\u002FmaxState\u002FargMaxState",")",[229,557,558,559],{},"Continuous aggregates with ",[250,560,561],{},"first\u002Flast",[208,563,564,567,570],{},[229,565,566],{},"Retention",[229,568,569],{},"TTL",[229,571,572],{},[250,573,574],{},"add_retention_policy",[188,576,577],{},"The watermark logic and the purge job would then be the database's job. Until a site needs more\nthan a few hundred hosts, the Frappe tables above are enough and keep Wolf a plain Frappe app.",{"title":579,"searchDepth":580,"depth":581,"links":582},"",1,2,[583,584,585,586,587,588],{"id":199,"depth":581,"text":200},{"id":342,"depth":581,"text":343},{"id":385,"depth":581,"text":386},{"id":408,"depth":581,"text":409},{"id":464,"depth":581,"text":173},{"id":472,"depth":581,"text":473},"How Wolf stores metrics at three resolutions, rolls them up, purges them and ingests pushes.","md",null,{},{"icon":171},{"title":168,"description":589},"9Mq_MGSo0IRLBz8NdrT7JJWehkdkyYBtmumMosRQQuk",[597,599],{"title":163,"path":164,"stem":165,"description":598,"icon":166},"The read and action APIs behind the Wolf UI at \u002Fwolf, their arguments, answers and access rules.",{"title":173,"path":174,"stem":175,"description":600,"icon":176},"Load test results at 100 hosts for 7 days, what changed to reach them, and how to run the test again.",1795104295106]